{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalCoordinateRing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalCoordinateRing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.AdjoinRoot","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Quotient","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.categorical_coordinate_ring_universal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.categorical_coordinate_ring_universal","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L98-L162","doc":"Universal property of `R[i, q^±¹]`: for any commutative `R`-algebra\n`S` equipped with a unit `qS : S^×` and an element `iS : S` with\n`iS^2 = -1`, there is a unique `R`-algebra homomorphism\n`R[i, q^±¹] → S` sending `q ↦ qS` and `i ↦ iS`.\n\nThe existence direction is the universal property of `AdjoinRoot`\nover `LaurentPolynomial`: build `LaurentR R →ₐ[R] S` sending `T 1 ↦ qS`\n(the monoid-algebra universal property, `AddMonoidAlgebra.lift`), make\n`S` a `LaurentR R`-algebra via it, then `AdjoinRoot.liftHom` with root\n`iS` (using `iS² = -1 ⟹ aeval iS (X²+1) = 0`) and `restrictScalars R`.\nUniqueness: any such `ψ` agrees with the constructed `φ` because it is\nforced to be `LaurentR R`-linear (two monoid homs from `Multiplicative ℤ`\nagreeing at `T 1 = qS`, `MonoidHom.ext_mint`), and then agrees on the\nroot `i_coord = iS` (`AdjoinRoot.algHom_ext`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.q_coord_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.q_coord_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L83-L90","doc":"The categorical coordinate `q` is a unit in `R[i, q^±¹]`.\nWitnessed explicitly by `q^{-1}` = image of `T (-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.i_coord_sq_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.i_coord_sq_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L71-L81","doc":"The defining identity `i^2 = -1` of the categorical coordinate `i`.\nFollows from `AdjoinRoot.eval_root`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.q_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.q_coord","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The categorical coordinate `q ∈ R[i, q^±¹]`, the chart-transition\ncoefficient of `P_q(V)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.i_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.i_coord","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The categorical coordinate `i ∈ R[i, q^±¹]`, the categorical\nsquare root of the antisymmetric braiding eigenvalue `λ_- = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateRing","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L48-L53","doc":"The categorical-coordinate ring `R[i, q^±¹] = R[q, q^{-1}][i]/(i^2+1)`.\n\nDeclared as an `abbrev` so the `CommRing`, `Algebra (LaurentR R) ·`,\nand `Algebra R ·` instances of `AdjoinRoot` transfer transparently. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-coordinate-ring","label":"prop:categorical-coordinate-ring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.iPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.iPoly","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L44-L46","doc":"The polynomial `i^2 + 1` over `R[q, q^{-1}]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.LaurentR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.LaurentR","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-coordinate-ring.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The ring `R[q, q^{-1}]` of Laurent polynomials in `q` over `R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}